# SSH client configuration.
#
# There are no private keys on this machine. 1Password holds them and exposes
# an agent socket; ssh asks that agent to sign, and the key itself never leaves
# the vault. That is why this file can be tracked in a public repo -- it names
# a socket, not a secret.

# FIRST, on purpose. ssh takes the FIRST value it obtains for each keyword, so
# anything in config.local wins over the block below. A missing file is fine.
Include ~/.ssh/config.local

Host *
  # 2BUA8C4S2C is AgileBits' Apple team ID, not per-user, which is why this is
  # tracked rather than generated. Quoted -- the path has spaces, and unquoted
  # ssh reads "Group" as the whole value and ignores the rest.
  IdentityAgent "~/Library/Group Containers/2BUA8C4S2C.com.1password/t/agent.sock"

  # Deliberately NOT `IdentitiesOnly yes`. It sounds like hardening and it
  # breaks this: it limits ssh to IdentityFile entries, of which there are
  # none, so nothing gets offered and you get Permission denied (publickey).
